        "U5"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "M6.3",
        "R40.1",
        "U11.18",
        "H7.1",
        "U5.24"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "/NET0046"
      ],
      "observed": "The KiCad netlist contains two distinct net entries with the same net name /NET0046. One entry connects the pH EZO SDA pin M6.3, the isolated I2C pull-up R40.1, and the ADM3260 secondary SDA pin U11.18. The other entry connects TMC2209 motor output OA1 U5.24 to stepper connector pin H7.1.",
      "expected": "The isolated pH I2C SDA net must remain separate from stepper-driver coil outputs. U5 OA1 should connect only to its motor coil connector net, not to M6/R40/U11 SDA.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"40\") (name \"/NET0046\") (node (ref \"M6\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"RX/SDA\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"46\") (name \"/NET0046\") (node (ref \"H7\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "U3 (pH) and U4 (EC) each present a secondary isolated I2C pair (`/SDA_pH`/`/SCL_pH`, `/SDA_EC`/`/SCL_EC`) that connects directly to M2 (EZO-pH) and M3 (EZO-EC) respectively"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "each drives a 2-phase coil output (`/A_xx+/-`, `/B_xx+/-`) to connectors H7/H8/H9"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "A motor coil output is merged with the isolated pH I2C bus. This corrupts pH communication, loads the I2C line with motor-driver switching, and can damage the ADM3260, EZO-pH circuit, or TMC2209 output when the pump is driven.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a clear bridged-net anomaly: net name /NET0046 is reused for both the pH isolated I2C SDA net and a TMC2209 motor coil output, merging unrelated signals."
}

